[{:db/id "q-37067/selection/da6ec38f87287c48f97b7f5538a006b7adbc63bec0be5e152accc6b9f3071e1b" :answer/id #uuid "aba7417d-1f6e-529f-9b3d-52057e3b050f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37067/selection/d2f31f4d56a14fc49eb3ecaa093fde943a0f070ed79fd2befe297508e545b824" :answer/id #uuid "c2f41616-8934-5a1b-bc98-40d0e6b12d15" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37067/selection/ae8c766ba6a4778188226fdbe40e47a3e0af4e9003f78e5609ad079821fd93a4" :answer/id #uuid "7b8b6a9c-0f11-5efb-a3b1-bb0f64a10ddd" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=-\\frac{1}{2}$, $x=-2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37067/selection/c80b56d2a172093828a40e322b923444eb35461b4314d5919758d8ff08f39b60" :answer/id #uuid "e410ab0a-4018-5a00-830b-b6d6ea8f35ac" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No vertical  asymptotes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37067/selection/244c82d9cc80c28419c5dc32926b80eb9b52caaf888f342ef093256f1875d75e" :answer/id #uuid "b30b5956-7a30-5fb5-8006-df94a7778e77" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{4}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-37067/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "092be388-8063-5ad5-8200-ae4d7df3d593" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-37067/selection/d2f31f4d56a14fc49eb3ecaa093fde943a0f070ed79fd2befe297508e545b824" :answer-field/choices ["q-37067/selection/da6ec38f87287c48f97b7f5538a006b7adbc63bec0be5e152accc6b9f3071e1b" "q-37067/selection/d2f31f4d56a14fc49eb3ecaa093fde943a0f070ed79fd2befe297508e545b824" "q-37067/selection/ae8c766ba6a4778188226fdbe40e47a3e0af4e9003f78e5609ad079821fd93a4" "q-37067/selection/c80b56d2a172093828a40e322b923444eb35461b4314d5919758d8ff08f39b60" "q-37067/selection/244c82d9cc80c28419c5dc32926b80eb9b52caaf888f342ef093256f1875d75e"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-37067" :question/id #uuid "3686a814-0b2c-5876-8371-9a4c81bce6f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-37067" :question/problem "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{2{x}^{2}+5x+2}.$" :question/worked-solution "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}-4}{2{x}^{2}+5x+2} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}-{2}^{2}}{2{x}^{2}+4x+x+2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+2)(x-2)}{2x(x+2)+(x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(x+2)(x-2)}{(2x+1)(x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{(x+2)}(x-2)}{(2x+1)\\cancel{(x+2)}} \\\\  & =\\frac{x-2}{2x+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n2x+1=0\\,⟹\\,x=-\\frac{1}{2}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the *only* vertical asymptote is at $x=-\\frac{1}{2}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-37067/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80b8388b-ae0b-5ea6-9efc-fed1a074f463"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-37067"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-73015/selection/4e6eeef5aa33ee4a1d2fff0c2887be5f32fe5006030d9cd9500bd4b039270d64" :answer/id #uuid "09572ae0-564c-57c5-9f08-8b47cb08f77f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73015/selection/16807e558f747c01804801b58893241f0ca0c4c58da13099858caa189ca296eb" :answer/id #uuid "ee0081b6-2731-5c0a-a317-e645442be93e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73015/selection/00258c5932d8286b792d219a898959e49995ba251596cc2f3ce2ad266e7bf98f" :answer/id #uuid "a6fb647c-8749-575f-99e9-003baba5b0be" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No vertical asymptotes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73015/selection/da6ec38f87287c48f97b7f5538a006b7adbc63bec0be5e152accc6b9f3071e1b" :answer/id #uuid "8103378b-163f-53c0-a4d8-5962d2ba5868" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73015/selection/04283b52ecee3637c693eb7a3782a2a357f47d9b9e2db64c850e377a3ee63036" :answer/id #uuid "a5cb0331-7ecd-5fd2-842d-39843f9e11b4" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=0$, $x=-2$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-73015/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "0601bd57-36b5-5a2f-9f81-e151b25b4bcf" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-73015/selection/00258c5932d8286b792d219a898959e49995ba251596cc2f3ce2ad266e7bf98f" :answer-field/choices ["q-73015/selection/4e6eeef5aa33ee4a1d2fff0c2887be5f32fe5006030d9cd9500bd4b039270d64" "q-73015/selection/16807e558f747c01804801b58893241f0ca0c4c58da13099858caa189ca296eb" "q-73015/selection/00258c5932d8286b792d219a898959e49995ba251596cc2f3ce2ad266e7bf98f" "q-73015/selection/da6ec38f87287c48f97b7f5538a006b7adbc63bec0be5e152accc6b9f3071e1b" "q-73015/selection/04283b52ecee3637c693eb7a3782a2a357f47d9b9e2db64c850e377a3ee63036"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-73015" :question/id #uuid "160272b1-97d5-53b9-bc93-753cba5d4e36" :question/math-academy-id "q-73015" :question/problem "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}{2x+4}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify the expression by factoring both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}{2x+4} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(x+2)}{2(x+2)}=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the denominator is never zero, we conclude that this function has no vertical asymptotes. A plot of the function is below. Note that it is not defined at $x=-2.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/assets/3ad83a79ccd47d9d035ac5a3f47b929a1e6b3939cdaddee9ff0f2d6a3cf07e56.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-73015/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "231604dc-fe8f-59be-90fe-37af7a1bb648"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-73015"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107038/selection/da6ec38f87287c48f97b7f5538a006b7adbc63bec0be5e152accc6b9f3071e1b" :answer/id #uuid "6d6d49e4-f011-5f80-a12a-4a933c6237a3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107038/selection/00258c5932d8286b792d219a898959e49995ba251596cc2f3ce2ad266e7bf98f" :answer/id #uuid "fdf2b4ff-1f6a-5796-97ce-063614d38def" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No vertical asymptotes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107038/selection/4e6eeef5aa33ee4a1d2fff0c2887be5f32fe5006030d9cd9500bd4b039270d64" :answer/id #uuid "f5428b4f-1422-5ae9-bf92-05116eae053a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107038/selection/6bac05a62229f29eba4498544257eb386a58da0ea736d3d95ca346c883c43950" :answer/id #uuid "cef396a3-1b21-5782-86a2-8a90b8121b34" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107038/selection/a74fdaba75fab23a42af138e3b01bfd2b38a6099e11ab377ae6a00bdb59a5022" :answer/id #uuid "7005cb60-66a4-5de3-8d19-4ad97561c698" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=-2,3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107038/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "8a440378-c4e7-5e4d-8eef-4099ec5e60ea" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107038/selection/00258c5932d8286b792d219a898959e49995ba251596cc2f3ce2ad266e7bf98f" :answer-field/choices ["q-107038/selection/da6ec38f87287c48f97b7f5538a006b7adbc63bec0be5e152accc6b9f3071e1b" "q-107038/selection/00258c5932d8286b792d219a898959e49995ba251596cc2f3ce2ad266e7bf98f" "q-107038/selection/4e6eeef5aa33ee4a1d2fff0c2887be5f32fe5006030d9cd9500bd4b039270d64" "q-107038/selection/6bac05a62229f29eba4498544257eb386a58da0ea736d3d95ca346c883c43950" "q-107038/selection/a74fdaba75fab23a42af138e3b01bfd2b38a6099e11ab377ae6a00bdb59a5022"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107038" :question/id #uuid "ffff2c65-4914-5cab-92fb-8939605d9866" :question/math-academy-id "q-107038" :question/problem "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{(x+2)({x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2})}{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}.$" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify the expression by factoring both the numerator and the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+2)({x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2})}{{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}} & =\\frac{{x}^{2}(x+2)({x}^{2}+x-6)}{{x}^{2}(x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{x}^{2}(x+2)}({x}^{2}+x-6)}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}(x+2)}} \\\\  & ={x}^{2}+x-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the denominator is never zero, we conclude that this function has no vertical asymptotes. A plot of the function is below. Note that it is not defined at $x=-2$ and $x=0.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14063519/assets/31f16682ad863f5f320130705ac57415a74340f3fe73a67a03b4df258c2577e7.png)" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-107038/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "231604dc-fe8f-59be-90fe-37af7a1bb648"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107038"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107075/selection/2f080de0ef65f6e5dd2806fa211066253fb2f37c1d406be458ab4efcf0eceed2" :answer/id #uuid "0920d4c7-131b-56a9-9939-37c13707b9e7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107075/selection/9f75d63bbce36d71b1687120236f1905d3381f1a10419d07fe4d39d3b5a3b550" :answer/id #uuid "274e5465-cc28-5c25-8cf6-a27dd4c265f8" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "$x=0$ and $x=1$" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107075/selection/00258c5932d8286b792d219a898959e49995ba251596cc2f3ce2ad266e7bf98f" :answer/id #uuid "2f183f20-972b-5974-852f-018f3b363cca" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No vertical asymptotes" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107075/selection/6bac05a62229f29eba4498544257eb386a58da0ea736d3d95ca346c883c43950" :answer/id #uuid "d8cf719b-1ced-52e4-a290-709d75a6a0a5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107075/selection/0bf5abed43f6f20dd466b36279de8736a04c540ff5306cb048ae22803a7b3f9c" :answer/id #uuid "086c9bf1-8b02-57c1-a86e-b5c780099044" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107075/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e619eb1a-dff4-5889-893b-fba716003d10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107075/selection/6bac05a62229f29eba4498544257eb386a58da0ea736d3d95ca346c883c43950" :answer-field/choices ["q-107075/selection/2f080de0ef65f6e5dd2806fa211066253fb2f37c1d406be458ab4efcf0eceed2" "q-107075/selection/9f75d63bbce36d71b1687120236f1905d3381f1a10419d07fe4d39d3b5a3b550" "q-107075/selection/00258c5932d8286b792d219a898959e49995ba251596cc2f3ce2ad266e7bf98f" "q-107075/selection/6bac05a62229f29eba4498544257eb386a58da0ea736d3d95ca346c883c43950" "q-107075/selection/0bf5abed43f6f20dd466b36279de8736a04c540ff5306cb048ae22803a7b3f9c"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107075" :question/id #uuid "9bd3afc4-6ef3-52a7-9d8b-591f71cdd447" :question/math-academy-id "q-107075" :question/problem "Find the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{5}{2x}+\\frac{3}{4x}.$" :question/worked-solution "First, let's put the two terms over a common denominator:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{5}{2x}+\\frac{3}{4x} & =\\frac{5(2)+3}{4x}=\\frac{13}{4x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we proceed to set the denominator equal to zero and get\n\n$$\n4x=0\\,⟹\\,x=0.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the vertical asymptotes are at $x=0.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-107075/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "68ba4c5d-8b91-57bc-b98b-0e9f8d8f1f67"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107075"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-339968/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer/id #uuid "03d36870-f66e-531f-92f2-7c5cb21b2088" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-339968/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f020e236-c3df-53b3-886d-2d973e9d2393" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-339968/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03" :answer-field/choices ["q-339968/field-1/be9eb51cc2f690a7d5b4aa400428edabf5a5d631a176c92b7f40bdd47725ed03"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-339968" :question/id #uuid "a0ab7f79-8620-5428-92fb-a584d8a11e91" :question/math-academy-id "q-339968" :question/problem "The vertical asymptote of $f(x)=\\frac{8x-16}{{x}^{2}-6x+8}$ is\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "We start by factoring the function as much as possible and canceling the common factors:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{8x-16}{{x}^{2}-6x+8} & =\\frac{8(x-2)}{(x-2)(x-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8\\cancel{(x-2)}}{\\cancel{(x-2)}(x-4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{8}{x-4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\nx-4=0\\,⟹\\,x=4\n$$\n\nSo the *only* vertical asymptote is at $x=4.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-339968/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "80b8388b-ae0b-5ea6-9efc-fed1a074f463"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-339968"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
